(436,1,'single_isSi','muiiiifakSi@olegrova-tatianas.site','https://single-calculator.com','87.199.207.10','2026-08-01 22:16:40','2026-08-01 22:16:40','OK — have been messing about with this thing for something like four months now and I keep coming back, so figured I\'d write something up since a mate asked me the other day. I\'m UK based, mainly do football and horses, a fiver here and there, for context. \r\n \r\nHow I found it was honestly embarrassing — I couldn\'t ever work out what an e/w payout would be when the place terms changed. Basically I\'d guess and then be surprised. These days I stick my stake in before I place anything, even a simple single bet. \r\n \r\nTheir single bet calculator tool is the one I\'m on daily — you put in stake and odds and it shows the return with no faffing, fractional or decimal, doesn\'t matter. It also handles the bigger stuff — doubles and trebles maths, a lucky 15, patents and yankees, and that\'s where I\'d always got it wrong. Have a go yourself, it\'s over at <a href=\"https://single-calculator.com/bet-calculator/each-way\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">ew bet calculator</a> — free, no signup. \r\n \r\nThe thing that genuinely changed how I bet is the geekier tools. There\'s an probability calculator that shows how much the bookie\'s taking, and a kelly criterion tool — I stick to fractional kelly because full kelly is far too aggressive. The dutching one gets used a fair bit when I\'m splitting a race. \r\n \r\nCouple of gripes. The layout feels pretty plain — no flash, which honestly I don\'t mind but some will. Phone-wise it\'s fine but the lucky 63 breakdown are a squeeze. And nothing on the app store, it\'s browser only — fine by me but you asked. \r\n \r\nRight, that\'s me. Free, barely any ads, works. If you still does the maths on paper, try it — saved me a fair few \"wait, that\'s it?\" moments.',0,'0','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/130.0.0.0 Safari/537.36','comm